  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Given name then family name. Many Estonian surnames are short nature or trade words given in the 1800s: Tamm (oak), Saar (island), Sepp (smith), Kukk (rooster). Estonian surnames are not gendered. Russian-speaking Estonians, about a quarter of the country and over a third of Tallinn, carry Russian names in Estonian spelling (Jelena, Mihhail, Vassiljev); women's surnames end in -ova or -eva, and patronymics are not used in everyday Estonian settings. Ukrainians arrived in large numbers from 2022. People use first names freely, and the formal 'teie' with strangers and elders.",
